<BaseLayout title="About — Ruijie Wu" description="About Ruijie Wu, psychotherapist and educator exploring body, movement and lived experience.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">About / 01</span>
    <h1>A life in dialogue<br /><em>with the body.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">I am Ruijie Wu (伍芮洁), a psychotherapist and educator interested in the ways our bodies, stories and relationships shape how we live.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="about-opening container">
    <div class="about-side-note">A little about<br />where I stand</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>My work brings together psychological thinking and embodied experience. I am drawn to the places where words become insufficient, where movement offers another language, and where a person can begin to encounter their experience with greater freedom.</p>
      <p>My clinical interests include trauma, grief and loss, cross-cultural transitions, identity and meaning-making. My approach is informed by existential-humanistic and feminist perspectives, alongside body-oriented and dance movement practices.</p>
      <p>I have studied and worked across China and France, and continue to explore how culture, history and lived experience are carried in the body.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">A continuing path</span><h2>Learning &amp;<br /><em>practice.</em></h2></div><p>Some coordinates in an ongoing journey of study, practice and inquiry.</p></div>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item"><span class="when">Psychology</span><div><strong>Applied Psychology</strong><p>Undergraduate training with a medical and psychological orientation.</p></div></div>
        <div class="timeline-item"><span class="when">Psychomotricity</span><div><strong>Psychomotor rehabilitation</strong><p>Graduate study in France, exploring the relationship between movement, body experience and psychological life.</p></div></div>
        <div class="timeline-item"><span class="when">Psychotraumatology</span><div><strong>Further study in trauma</strong><p>Specialised academic training at Université Paris Cité.</p></div></div>
        <div class="timeline-item"><span class="when">Dance &amp; movement</span><div><strong>Dance Movement Therapy</strong><p>Ongoing professional development at the intersection of dance, psychology and embodied practice.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
